      "knowledge_point": "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function",
      "problem": "Find the derivative of  $f(t)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t\\,i+(3{t}^{2}-5t)\\,j+\\frac{1}{1+t}\\,k$ at $t=1.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-5t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{1+t})\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}\\,i+(6t-5)\\,j-\\frac{1}{(1+t)^{2}}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{′}(1)$ we substitute $t=1$ into the expression for ${f}^{′}(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{1}{1+(1)^{2}}\\,i+(6(1)-5)\\,j-\\frac{1}{(1+(1))^{2}}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\,j-\\frac{1}{4}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$",
